; bfsodium SHA3_256 : FIPS 202 section 6  the sponge over Keccak_f{1600}
;
; HAND WRITTEN; The permutation is keccak/permute1600  PASTED  and entered once
; per block of the padded message and never again  because thirty two bytes of
; answer fit inside one rate;
;
; INTERFACE entry=1 exit=0 footprint=0:1020
; IO  in:  mlen{2} LE  then mlen bytes from the wire
;     out: digest{32}
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x0c7  S{200}  the sponge state; it starts at NOUGHT  which is why
;                         the two length bytes are moved up out of it below
;   @0x0c8:0x330  keccak/permute1600's frame  pasted at this file's own zero
;   @0x338:0x3bf  BB{136} the block being filled; one RATE of the sponge
;   @0x3c8:0x3ed  the exclusive or frame; xor64 pasted at @0x3c8
;   @0x3f0        mlo     message bytes still to come  low byte
;   @0x3f1        mhi     and high byte
;   @0x3f2        msgleft one while either of those is not nought
;   @0x3f3        pad     one until the padding byte has been placed
;   @0x3f4        more    one while another block is wanted
;   @0x3f5        ic      the hundred and thirty six bytes of a block
;   @0x3f6:0x3fb  t0 t1 e0 t2 t3 e1  the cells the four tests are made through
;   @0x3fc        last    one if the padding byte was placed in THIS block
;
; THE RATE IS A HUNDRED AND THIRTY SIX and that is exactly SEVENTEEN LANES  so
; absorbing a block is seventeen entries of xor64 rather than a hundred and
; thirty six byte exclusive ors; Every rate in the family divides by eight the
; same way: 168 for SHAKE128 is twenty one lanes  136 for SHAKE256 and SHA3_256
; is seventeen  and 72 for SHA3_512 is nine;
;
; AND EVERY OPERAND IS MOVED  never copied  which is the one place this file is
; cheaper than keccak/theta: the state lane is replaced by the answer and the
; block is spent  so nothing needs handing back;
;
; THE BLOCK IS FILLED BY A CONVEYOR  because there is no index: a byte always
; enters at the TOP of the block and the block slides down one before the next
; one arrives; So the byte that enters first has slid a hundred and thirty five
; times when the block is full and comes to rest at the bottom  which is where
; it belongs; poly1305/absorb fills its sixteen byte block the same way;
;
; THE PADDING IS FIPS 202's  and the conveyor makes it almost free: when the
; message runs out the next byte to enter is 6  and after that nothing enters
; at all  which leaves noughts behind the conveyor exactly as the rule wants;
; The last byte of the LAST block then gains 128; That byte is either nought or
; the 6 itself  so the addition cannot carry  and the case where the message is
; a whole number of blocks needs no special arm: the padding simply gets a block
; of its own;
;
; ON THE LAST BLOCK AND NOT ON EVERY BLOCK  which is worth saying because the
; first version of this file did it on every one and only failed once a message
; was long enough to need two; The block in which the padding byte was placed is
; the last block by definition  so placing it sets a flag and the 128 is added
; under that flag;
;
; A BLOCK IS ABOUT FOUR BILLION INSTRUCTIONS  nearly all of it the permutation
; at three thousand nine hundred and thirty nine million  so nothing else in
; this file is worth optimising until that is; The conveyor costs about five
; million per block and the absorb twenty five  which together are under one
; percent of it;
;
; The length is read into the bottom two cells of the STATE and moved up out of
; it  because a read prologue may hold nothing but commas and steps and the
; state must start at nought; Every distance below was worked out from the map;

; read the message length little endian
  ,>,
